# Generated export with unstable line order — the 5 `bd remember` memory records
# come out of a Go map, so every bd command reshuffles them. `clean` canonicalises
# to sorted order so git never sees the churn; `merge` unions by record id so
# branches touching unrelated issues don't collide. Both need the one-time
# `git config` per clone documented in CLAUDE.md — an unconfigured driver or
# filter is silently skipped.
.beads/issues.jsonl merge=beads-jsonl filter=beads-jsonl
